## Why This Is Asked

This question probes hands-on experience building streaming joins with per-key state, TTL-based invalidation, and robust delivery guarantees in KCNA-like pipelines.

## Key Concepts

- Per-sensor TTL cache
- Event-time join with watermarks
- Side-input-driven re-enrichment
- Offset tracking and at-least-once semantics

## Code Example

```java
// Pseudo KCNA sink skeleton
class CalibratedJoinSink {
  Map<String, Calibration> cache;
  void onCalibration(Calibration c){ cache.put(c.sensorId, c); }
  void onReading(Reading r){
    Calibration c = cache.get(r.sensorId);
    r.factor = (c != null) ? c.factor : 1.0;
    emit(r);
    // optionally track buffered items for late calibration
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to handle calibration TTL expiry without missed re-enrichment?
- How to test robustness under high-cardinality sensors and bursty data?

